\p When¦85284 the¦85285 chief¦85286 priest¦85286 arrived¦85282 with¦85289 his companions, they¦85295 called¦85295 together¦85295 the¦85297 \add religious\add* council¦85298 and¦85299 also¦85299 the¦85301 \add political\add* council¦85302 of Yisrael¦85305, then¦85306 called for¦85312 the missionaries to¦85311 be¦85311 brought¦85311 in from the¦85309 prison¦85310.
\v 22 But¦85314 when their attendants¦85319 got¦85316 to the¦85327 jail, they weren't there, so¦85330 they returned¦85329 to the gathering and told them,
\v 23 “We¦85338 found¦85338 the prison¦85337 all¦85342 locked up with the¦85345 guards¦85346 in their positions at the¦85351 doors¦85352, but¦85354 when¦85344 they opened¦85353 it up¦85353, there was no¦85356 one¦85356 inside¦85355!”
\v 24 When¦85358 they¦85360 heard¦85360 this¦85383, the¦85364 officer¦85369 of¦85370 the¦85370 temple¦85371 and¦85372 the¦85373 chief¦85374 priests¦85374 were¦85375 totally puzzled¦85375 as to what¦85379 could have happened.
\v 25 Just then someone¦85386 came¦85384 in and told them¦85388, “Hey, the¦85392 men¦85393 that¦85390 you¦85395 put¦85395 in¦85396 prison¦85398 are¦85399 in¦85400 the¦85401 temple¦85402—standing¦85403 there teaching¦85405 the¦85406 people¦85407.”
