\v 1 However around that time¦85822 when¦85819 the¦85821 number of Yeshua-followers were growing, some of the¦85825 Greek converts starting grumbling¦85828 about¦85829 the Jewish believers because¦85834 the¦85842 \add @Greek\add* widows¦85843 were¦85835 being¦85835 overlooked¦85835 in¦85837 the¦85840 daily¦85841 sharing \add of food and money\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈So¦85851\add* the¦85852 twelve¦85853 \add missionaries\add* assembled the believers together and told¦85858 them, “We're not¦85861 pleased¦85862 about having¦85866 to take time off \add sharing\add* the¦85868 message¦85869 \nd of¦85871 God¦85871\nd* to¦85872 be¦85872 serving¦85872 here at the \add distribution\add* tables¦85873.
\v 3 So brothers¦85881, look around you¦85885 for seven¦85889 men¦85883 who are well known to be full¦85890 \nd of¦85891\nd* \add &God's¦85891\add* \nd spirit¦85891\nd* and¦85893 wisdom¦85894, so we¦85896 can appoint¦85896 them to be¦85896 \add ≈in charge of\add* this¦85902 part of the work.
\v 4 Then we¦85903 \add ourselves\add* can continue to pray¦85907 and¦85908 share the¦85911 message¦85912.”
\p
\v 5 This idea pleased¦85916 the¦85923 group, so¦85927 they¦85928 went ahead¦85920 and chose¦85928 Stephen¦85931 (a¦85932 man¦85932 full¦85933 of¦85935 faith¦85935 and¦85937 \nd of¦85938 the¦85938\nd* holy¦85940 \nd spirit¦85938\nd*), Philip¦85942, Procorus, Nikanor¦85946, Timon¦85948, Parmenas¦85950, and¦85951 Nicolas¦85952 (a¦85953 non-Jew from¦85954 Antioch¦85954 who had previously converted¦85953 to Judaism).
\v 6 They¦85958 stood¦85958 these seven up \add ≈in¦85961 front¦85961 of¦85961\add* the¦85962 missionaries¦85963, who prayed¦85966 and then placed¦85967 their¦85969 hands¦85970 on¦85968 them¦85968.
