\p
\v 8 Now Stephen¦85999 \add (one of the seven)\add* was full¦86001 of¦86002 grace¦86002 and¦86004 power¦86005 and was¦86006 doing¦86006 miracles¦86007 and¦86008 amazing demonstrations of God's power among¦86011 the¦86012 people¦86013.
\v 9 But¦86021 a group from the Freedmen¦86031 Synagogue¦86026 as well as \add Jews\add* from¦86033 Cyrene¦86033, Alexandria, Cilicia¦86039, and¦86040 Asia¦86041 \add Minor\add* rose¦86020 up¦86020 and started arguing¦86042 against Stephen¦86044,
\v 10 but¦86045 they¦86048 weren't able¦86048 to¦86049 refute the¦86050 wisdom¦86051 that he¦86062 spoke¦86062 \add with the help of\add* the¦86057 pure \nd spirit¦86058\nd*.
\v 11 So they¦86079 got some men¦86080 \add to falsely accuse Stephen\add* saying¦86081, “We¦86084 heard¦86084 him¦86085 denigrating¦86090 Mosheh¦86092 and¦86093 \nd God¦86095\nd*.”
