\v 14 because¦86146 we¦86145 heard¦86145 him¦86147 saying¦86148 that¦86149 that¦86153 \nd Yeshua¦86150\nd* from¦86152 Nazaret¦86152 will¦86154 be¦86154 tearing¦86154 down¦86154 this¦86157 building and¦86158 will¦86159 be¦86159 changing¦86159 the¦86160 traditions¦86162 that¦86163 Mosheh¦86166 gave¦86164 to¦86165 us¦86165.”
\v 15 \add ≈So\add* then the¦86180 council¦86181 members looked¦86168 across at¦86171 \add @Stephen¦86172\add* and saw¦86183 that his¦86186 face¦86188 \add was shining\add* like that of¦86189 one \add of\add* \add &God's¦86189\add* \add #messengers¦86189\add*.
\c 7
\s1 Stephen's history discourse and accusations
\rem /s1 Stephen's Speech to the Council; Stephen's Speech to the Sanhedrin; Stephen Addresses the Council
\p
\v 1 Then¦86195 the¦86196 chief¦86197 priest¦86197 asked¦86194 \add Stephen\add*, “Is¦86205 all this true?”
\p
\v 2 And¦86207 he¦86206 replied¦86208, “My brothers¦86211 and¦86212 fathers¦86213, please listen¦86214. Our honoured \nd God¦86216\nd* was¦86219 seen¦86219 by¦86220 our ancestor Abraham¦86223 in¦86225 Mesopotamia¦86227 before¦86228 he moved to¦86230 Haran¦86233
\v 3 and¦86234 he¦86235 told¦86235 him¦86237, ‘Leave your land¦86242 and¦86244 your relatives¦86247, and¦86249 go to¦86251 the¦86252 place that I¦86258 will¦86258 show¦86258 you¦86257.’\x + \xo 7:2-3: \xt Gen 12:1.\x*
\v 4 So he¦86266 left Chaldea and moved to Haran¦86268,\x + \xo 7:4: \xt Gen 11:31.\x* and¦86269 then¦86259 after¦86272 his¦86277 father¦86276 died¦86274, he¦86279 moved again to¦86281 this¦86284 land¦86283 where \add %we¦86287\add* now¦86288 live¦86289.\x + \xo 7:4: \xt Gen 12:4.\x*
\v 5 \add @Abraham¦86300\add* hadn't received any land here as an¦86301 inheritance¦86301, in¦86302 fact he'd never been near this land and nor¦86304 did he have any \add #children¦86328\add*, yet \add @God\add* promised¦86309 to¦86311 give¦86311 this \add entire\add* country to¦86312 him¦86312 and¦86318 his¦86321 descendants¦86320.\x + \xo 7:5: \xt Gen 12:7; 13:15; 15:18; 17:8.\x*
\v 6 And yet \nd God¦86334\nd* \add also\add* told¦86329 him that¦86337 his¦86342 descendants¦86340 would end up staying in¦86344 another country¦86345 where they¦86348 would¦86348 be¦86348 enslaved¦86348 and¦86351 mistreated¦86352 for four¦86355 hundred¦86355 years¦86354.
\v 7 However \nd God¦86369\nd* promised to punish the¦86357 nation¦86359 that enslaved them, and¦86371 told¦86370 him that in the end they¦86374 would¦86374 leave that place¦86381 and¦86375 serve¦86376 him here in¦86379 this¦86382 country.\x + \xo 7:6-7: \xt Gen 15:13-14.\x*\x + \xo 7:7: \xt Exo 3:12.\x*
\v 8 And¦86383 he¦86384 contracted with \add @Abraham¦86385\add* about¦86387 being circumcised¦86387,\x + \xo 7:8: \xt Gen 17:10-14.\x* and¦86388 so¦86389 when \add @Abraham¦86390\add* had Isaac¦86392, he circumcised¦86394 him¦86395 on¦86396 the¦86398 eighth¦86400 day¦86397,\x + \xo 7:8: \xt Gen 21:2-4.\x* and¦86401 then Isaac¦86403 went on to have Yacob¦86405,\x + \xo 7:8: \xt Gen 25:26.\x* and¦86406 Yacob¦86408 to have the \add twelve\add* tribal leaders.\x + \xo 7:8: \xt Gen 29:31–35:18.\x*
\p
\v 9 Those brothers went on to become jealous¦86415 of¦86417 Yosef¦86417\x + \xo 7:9: \xt Gen 37:11.\x* and sent him back¦86418 into¦86419 Egypt¦86420 \add as a slave\add*,\x + \xo 7:9: \xt Gen 37:28.\x* but¦86421 \nd God¦86424\nd* was¦86422 with¦86425 him¦86426\x + \xo 7:9: \xt Gen 39:2,21.\x*
\v 10 and¦86427 rescued¦86428 him¦86429 out¦86430 of¦86430 all¦86431 his¦86434 troubles there. Then¦86435 \add @God\add* gave¦86436 him¦86437 wisdom¦86441 and caused him to gain the favour¦86438 of \add Far'oh (Pharaoh)\add*, the king¦86445 of¦86446 Egypt¦86446, who then¦86447 appointed¦86448 him¦86449 as the ruler of all Egypt¦86452 and¦86453 over¦86454 Far'oh's¦86444 own household¦86457.\x + \xo 7:10: \xt Gen 41:39-41.\x*
\v 11 Then¦86461 a¦86462 famine¦86462 hit all¦86464 Egypt¦86470 and¦86471 Canaan¦86472 causing great¦86475 distress and¦86476 our¦86482 ancestors¦86481 were¦86478 unable to find¦86478 enough food¦86479.\x + \xo 7:11: \xt Gen 42:1-2.\x*
\v 12 But¦86485 Yacob¦86486 heard¦86483 that grain¦86488 was available in¦86490 Egypt¦86492, so first¦86501, he sent¦86494 off our¦86500 tribal leaders.
\v 13 On¦86504 \add &their¦86505\add* second¦86506 visit, Yosef¦86509 revealed himself to¦86518 them,\x + \xo 7:13: \xt Gen 45:1.\x* and¦86513 so Far'oh¦86518 \add ≈became¦86515 aware\add* of¦86523 Yosef's¦86523 heritage.\x + \xo 7:13: \xt Gen 45:16.\x*
\v 14 Then¦86525 Yosef¦86526 sent¦86524 for his¦86531 father¦86530 Yacob¦86528 and¦86533 all¦86534 the¦86535 extended family\x + \xo 7:14: \xt Gen 45:9-10,17-18.\x*—some seventy-five of them.\x + \xo 7:14: \xt Gen 46:27 (LXX).\x*
\v 15 \add ≈So¦86544\add* Yacob¦86547 went¦86545 to¦86548 Egypt¦86549,\x + \xo 7:15: \xt Gen 46:1-7.\x* where he¦86552 and¦86554 the¦86555 \add twelve\add* tribal leaders \add eventually\add* died¦86551,\x + \xo 7:15: \xt Gen 49:33.\x*
\v 16 although their bodies were¦86559 moved to¦86561 Shekem¦86562 where they¦86564 were¦86564 put¦86564 into¦86565 the¦86566 tomb¦86567 that¦86569 Abraham¦86571 had bought¦86570 from¦86574 the¦86575 sons¦86576 of¦86577 Hamor¦86577.\x + \xo 7:16: \xt Gen 23:3-16; 33:19; 50:7-13; Josh 24:32.\x*
\p
\v 17 But¦86584 as¦86583 the¦86586 time¦86588 limit promised¦86593 to¦86598 Abraham¦86598 by \nd God¦86596\nd* was¦86585 getting closer, \add &our¦86600\add* people¦86601 multiplied¦86603 in¦86604 Egypt¦86605\x + \xo 7:17-18: \xt Exo 1:7-8.\x*
\v 18 until¦86606 another¦86610 Far'oh \add !(Pharaoh)\add* ended up¦86608 ruling \add *there\add* who¦86613 had¦86616 never known¦86616 Yosef¦86619.
\v 19 He took¦86623 advantage¦86623 of¦86624 us¦86626 Jews and mistreated¦86627 our ancestors¦86629,\x + \xo 7:19: \xt Exo 1:10-11.\x* even forcing them apart from their¦86637 own babies¦86635 so they wouldn't live¦86641.\x + \xo 7:19: \xt Exo 1:22.\x*
\v 20 Mosheh¦86647 was¦86646 born¦86646 during that¦86643 time¦86644 and¦86648 \nd God¦86652\nd* considered him beautiful¦86650. He spent three¦86656 months¦86655 in¦86657 his \add own\add* father's¦86661 house¦86659\x + \xo 7:20: \xt Exo 2:2.\x*
\v 21 before being¦86665 placed¦86665 outside¦86665, from where Far'oh's¦86676 daughter¦86675 took¦86672 him¦86673 and¦86677 brought¦86678 him¦86679 up¦86678 herself¦86681 as her own son¦86683.\x + \xo 7:21: \xt Exo 2:3-10.\x*
\v 22 \add ≈So¦86684\add* Mosheh¦86686 was¦86685 instructed¦86685 in all¦86688 the¦86691 wisdom¦86691 of¦86693 the¦86693 Egyptians, and¦86696 was¦86694 a powerful¦86697 speaker and¦86700 project leader.
\p
\v 23 But¦86705 when¦86704 he hit forty¦86710, it entered his¦86716 \add ≈mind¦86715\add* to¦86717 visit¦86717 his¦86720 relatives¦86719, the¦86721 Israelis¦86723.\x + \xo 7:23-29: \xt Exo 2:11-15.\x*
\v 24 When¦86724 he noticed¦86725 one¦86726 of them being¦86727 mistreated, he¦86731 retaliated¦86731 and¦86733 while defending the¦86736 oppressed man, he struck¦86738 \add and killed\add* the¦86739 Egyptian¦86740.
\v 25 He¦86747 thought¦86747 \add &his¦86751\add* relatives¦86752 would understand¦86750 that¦86754 \nd God¦86756\nd* was¦86760 bringing salvation¦86762 to¦86763 them¦86763 via him, but¦86766 they¦86764 didn't¦86767 see it that way.
\v 26 \add ≈So¦86771\add* on¦86770 the¦86770 following¦86772 day¦86773 when he¦86774 saw¦86774 two of them¦86775 quarrelling¦86776, he¦86783 tried to¦86787 resolve the situation by saying¦86789, ‘Men¦86792, you're¦86794 all¦86794 brothers¦86793. Why¦86797 are¦86798 you¦86798 injuring¦86798 each other?’
\v 27 But¦86802 the¦86801 bullying one pushed¦86806 him¦86807 away¦86806 and said¦86808, ‘Who¦86809 made you¦86810 the judge¦86814 over¦86815 us¦86817?
\v 28 Do you¦86821 want¦86822 to¦86819 kill¦86819 me¦86820 like you¦86825 killed¦86825 that¦86823 Egyptian¦86828 yesterday¦86826?’
\v 29 When¦86834 he heard that¦86839, Mosheh¦86835 fled¦86833 \add Egypt\add* and¦86840 became¦86841 an exile in¦86843 Midian¦86845 where¦86846 he¦86847 \add eventually\add* had two¦86849 sons¦86848.\x + \xo 7:29: \xt Exo 18:3-4.\x*
\p
\v 30 After another forty¦86858 years¦86856, he was¦86853 in¦86861 the¦86862 wilderness¦86863 around Mt¦86865. Sinai¦86867 when¦86850 he saw¦86859 a¦86868 messenger¦86868 in the flame¦86871 of¦86875 a¦86875 burning¦86872 thorn¦86875 bush¦86875.\x + \xo 7:30-34: \xt Exo 3:1-10.\x*
\v 31 Mosheh¦86878 was amazed¦86880 at¦86882 the¦86882 vision¦86883 when he saw¦86879 it¦86879, so¦86886 he approached¦86885 \add the bush\add* to¦86889 look more closely when he heard Yahweh's voice¦86891 saying,
\v 32 ‘I¦86900 am¦86900 the¦86901 \nd god¦86902\nd* of¦86903 your¦86905 ancestors¦86904—the¦86906 \nd god¦86907\nd* of¦86908 Abraham¦86908 and¦86909 of¦86912 Isaac¦86912 and¦86913 of¦86916 Yacob¦86916.’ At that point, Mosheh¦86921 started trembling¦86917 and was¦86924 scared to go any closer to look,
\v 33 but¦86931 \nd Yahweh¦86936\nd* said¦86928, ‘Take off your¦86945 \add #sandals¦86940\add*, because¦86947 the¦86946 ground¦86956 you're¦86955 standing¦86955 on is¦86958 dedicated¦86957 to God.
\v 34 I have¦86960 noticed¦86962 the¦86963 mistreatment¦86964 of¦86965 my¦86967 people¦86966 in¦86969 Egypt¦86970 and¦86971 heard¦86976 their¦86974 groaning¦86973 and¦86978 so I¦86979 came¦86979 down¦86979 to¦86980 rescue¦86980 them¦86981, so¦86982 now¦86983 I'm¦86985 going to send¦86985 you¦86987 \add back\add* to¦86988 Egypt¦86989.’
\p
\v 35 This¦86990 was the¦86991 same Mosheh¦86992 that they¦86994 had¦86995 previously rejected and asked¦86995 who¦86996 had made \add %him¦86997\add* ruler¦86999 and¦87000 judge¦87001 over them.\x + \xo 7:35: \xt Exo 2:14.\x* \add Now\add* \nd God¦87006\nd* had¦87014 indeed sent¦87014 him as ruler¦87008 and¦87010 liberator by means of¦87018 the¦87018 messenger¦87018 that¦87019 he saw¦87020 in¦87022 the¦87023 thorn¦87024 bush¦87024.
\v 36 So \add eventually\add* \add @Mosheh\add* led¦87026 them¦87027 out¦87026 of Egypt¦87036 after doing¦87029 miracles¦87030 and¦87031 signs¦87032 of God's power there,\x + \xo 7:36: \xt Exo 7:3.\x* and¦87038 then also at the¦87040 Red¦87040 Sea¦87041\x + \xo 7:36: \xt Exo 14:21.\x* and¦87042 during¦87043 the¦87044 forty¦87047 years¦87046 in the wilderness¦87045.\x + \xo 7:36: \xt Num 14:33.\x*
\v 37 This¦87048 same Mosheh¦87051 told¦87053 Israelis¦87056 that in the future \nd God¦87062\nd* would¦87059 raise¦87059 up¦87059 another prophet¦87057 like¦87070 \add %him¦87058\add* from¦87065 among \add %them\add*.\x + \xo 7:37: \xt Deu 18:15,18.\x*
\v 38 Now \add @Mosheh\add* was¦87076 the¦87077 person¦87077 that \add led\add* the¦87080 assembly¦87081 \add of people\add* in¦87082 the¦87083 wilderness¦87084, was spoken¦87089 to by one \add of\add* \add &God's\add* \add #messengers¦87087\add* on¦87091 Mt¦87093. Sinai¦87094, and¦87095 one of¦87096 our¦87099 ancestors¦87097 that¦87100 received¦87102 living¦87105 messages to¦87106 pass¦87106 on¦87106 to¦87107 \add %us¦87107\add*.\x + \xo 7:38: \xt Exo 19:1–20:17; Deu 5:1-33.\x*
\p
\v 39 “Yet our¦87117 ancestors¦87116 didn't¦87111 want to¦87114 obey¦87113 that man, so they¦87119 rejected him and¦87120 started thinking about¦87131 Egypt¦87133 again,
