\v 14 One of them was Lydia¦94994 from Thyatira¦94998 who was a¦94995 seller¦94995 of¦94995 purple¦94995 goods\f + \fr 16:14 \ft It's possible that Lydia dyed fabric and sold it, or that she actually made and sold the purple dye itself.\f* and although she already worshipped¦94999 \nd God¦95002\nd*, the¦95006 \nd master¦95007\nd* opened¦95008 her¦95009 \add ≈mind¦95010\add* and she \add readily\add* accepted¦95011 what Paul¦95016 was saying.
\v 15 \add ≈So¦95018\add* then¦95017 \add @Lydia¦95019\add* and her¦95024 household were¦95019 all \add ceremonially\add* immersed¦95019, and¦95020 then she¦95025 requested, “If¦95027 you¦95028 all¦95028 consider me¦95029 to¦95034 be¦95034 faithful¦95030 to¦95031 the¦95031 \nd master¦95033\nd*, come¦95035 and stay¦95042 at my¦95041 place.” So¦95044 she¦95045 persuaded us¦95047.
\s1 Paul and Silas get thrown into prison
\rem /s1 In Prison at Philippi; Paul and Silas in Prison
\p
\v 16 One time as we were walking¦95050 to¦95052 the¦95053 prayer¦95054 meeting, we met a¦95055 female slave¦95055 who¦95066 was possessed by a¦95059 spirit¦95059 that enabled her to tell fortunes, and thanks to that¦95066, to earn a lot of money for¦95071 her masters¦95072.
\v 17 She walked along behind \add *us\add* and¦95083 shouted¦95086 out¦95086, “These¦95089 men¦95091 are¦95097 slaves¦95092 \nd of¦95094\nd* the¦95095 highest¦95096 \nd god¦95094\nd* and they will be¦95100 telling¦95100 you¦95101 all¦95101 how to be saved.”
\v 18 After she'd¦95107 done¦95107 this¦95105 for¦95108 several¦95109 days¦95110, Paul¦95115 was¦95112 so¦95116 frustrated that he turned¦95117 around¦95118 and spoke¦95122 to the¦95118 spirit¦95119 \add in her\add*, “I¦95123 command¦95123 you¦95124 by the¦95127 \add ≈authority\add* \nd of¦95128 Yeshua¦95128 the¦95129 messiah¦95129\nd* to¦95131 leave her¦95134.”
\p
\v 19 But¦95148 when her¦95152 masters¦95151 realised¦95146 that¦95155 their¦95162 profitable business¦95161 was about¦95162 to \add ≈come¦95156 to an end\add*, they grabbed¦95167 Paul¦95169 and¦95170 Silas¦95172 and dragged¦95173 them¦95173 to¦95174 the authorities at the¦95175 marketplace¦95176.
\v 20 They brought¦95181 them¦95183 forward¦95181 to¦95184 face the¦95184 magistrates and said¦95186, “These¦95187 Jews¦95195 are¦95190 disturbing¦95190 \add the peace\add* in our¦95192 city¦95194
\v 21 and¦95197 teaching behaviour that¦95202 we as Romans¦95212 can neither accept¦95207 nor¦95210 practice¦95211.”
\v 22 An \add angry\add* crowd¦95219 gathered around and¦95225 the¦95226 magistrates ordered for \add @Paul and Silas\add* to have¦95228 their¦95229 robes¦95231 torn¦95228 off¦95228 and then to¦95233 be¦95233 beaten¦95233 with¦95233 rods¦95233.
\v 23 They¦95240 were severely beaten and¦95236 then thrown¦95240 into¦95241 prison¦95242 where the officer was commanded¦95243 to¦95246 keep¦95249 them¦95251 secure¦95248.
\v 24 Because of that¦95252, he threw¦95260 them¦95261 into¦95262 the¦95263 inner¦95264 cell and¦95266 locked¦95270 their¦95267 feet¦95268 in¦95273 stocks¦95277.
\p
\v 25 Around midnight¦95282 Paul¦95287 and¦95288 Silas¦95290 were praying¦95291 and singing¦95292 praises \nd to¦95294 God¦95294\nd*, and¦95296 the¦95299 other prisoners¦95301 were¦95295 listening¦95295 to¦95297 them¦95297.
\v 26 Suddenly¦95302 there was a strong earthquake¦95304 that¦95307 shook¦95308 even the¦95309 foundations¦95310 of¦95311 the¦95311 prison¦95312, and¦95314 immediately¦95316 all¦95319 the¦95317 prison doors¦95318 opened¦95313 up¦95313 and¦95320 the¦95322 chains¦95323 of¦95321 all¦95321 the prisoners came loose.
\v 27 The¦95330 prison¦95331 officer woke¦95327 up¦95334, and¦95332 when he saw¦95333 that all the¦95335 prison doors¦95336 were¦95334 open¦95334, he drew¦95341 his¦95342 sword¦95343 to take his own life as he figured that all the¦95350 prisoners¦95351 must have¦95349 escaped¦95349.
\v 28 But¦95353 Paul¦95359 shouted out, “Don't harm¦95365 yourself¦95363! We're¦95368 all¦95366 \add still\add* here¦95369!”
\p
\v 29 The officer called for torches, then¦95372 rushed¦95375 in¦95375 and¦95376 knelt down trembling¦95377 \add ≈in¦95380 front¦95380 of¦95380\add* Paul¦95385 and¦95386 Silas¦95388.
\v 30 Then¦95389 he escorted them¦95393 out¦95394 and asked¦95400, “Masters¦95402, what¦95403 do¦95406 I¦95408 need to do to be¦95408 saved¦95408?”
\p
\v 31 “Believe¦95412 in¦95414 the¦95415 \nd master¦95416 Yeshua¦95417\nd*,” they replied¦95411, “then¦95419 you¦95421 and¦95422 your¦95425 household¦95424 can all be saved¦95420.”
\v 32 Then¦95426 they¦95427 explained the¦95429 message¦95430 about¦95431 the¦95431 \nd master¦95433\nd* to¦95428 him¦95428 and all¦95436 those in¦95438 his¦95441 household¦95440.
\v 33 Even though it was still the¦95448 middle of¦95450 the¦95450 night¦95451, he¦95453 sponged their¦95455 wounds¦95456, and¦95457 then him and¦95462 his¦95467 household were all¦95469 immersed¦95459 straight away.
\v 34 He took¦95473 \add @Paul¦95476 and¦95476 Silas¦95476\add* up¦95473 into¦95477 \add &his¦95478\add* house¦95479 and gave them a¦95483 meal, and¦95484 \add &his¦95490\add* whole¦95490 household¦95490 were happy because they now believed¦95492 \nd in¦95496 God¦95496\nd*.
\p
\v 35 The next day¦95498 the¦95503 magistrates sent¦95502 officials¦95505 to tell¦95523 the jailer to release¦95526 \add @Paul and Silas\add*.
\p
