\v 37 But¦95563 Paul¦95564 responded¦95565, “You mean that after publicly¦95571 beating¦95569 us¦95570 Roman¦95574 men¦95573 without a trial, they¦95578 threw¦95578 us¦95578 into¦95579 prison¦95580 and¦95581 now¦95582 they¦95585 want to just quietly¦95583 release us.”
\p
\v 38 \add ≈So¦95595\add* the¦95601 officials¦95600 reported¦95593 this back to¦95599 the¦95599 magistrates, and¦95616 they¦95614 were¦95614 quite afraid¦95614 when they heard¦95617 that¦95618 \add @Paul¦95620 and¦95620 Silas¦95620\add* were¦95620 Roman¦95619 \add citizens\add*.
\v 39 \add ≈So¦95622\add* now they came¦95623 to the prison in person, and appealed¦95631 to¦95632 them¦95632, and¦95643 escorting them out¦95644 of prison themselves, asked¦95645 them¦95645 to¦95649 please leave¦95649 the¦95653 city¦95654.
