\p
\v 1 After travelling¦95691 through¦95691 Amphipolis¦95695 and¦95696 Apollonia¦95698, \add @Paul¦95699 and¦95699 Silas¦95699\add* went¦95699 to¦95704 Thessalonica¦95706 where¦95707 there was¦95708 a¦95710 \add ≈Jewish¦95710 meeting¦95710 hall¦95710\add*.
\v 2 Paul's¦95720 custom was to¦95714 attend at the¦95716 \add local\add* meeting hall on the¦95718 Rest¦95727 Day¦95727, so he¦95722 did that, and¦95725 for¦95726 three¦95728 weekends in a row he¦95729 discussed¦95729 the¦95735 scriptures¦95736 with them,
\v 3 showing them how that¦95740 it¦95743 \add had been written\add* that the¦95741 \nd messiah¦95742\nd* would suffer¦95744 and be killed and \add ≈come back to¦95746 life\add*, and¦95749 then explaining, “This¦95751 \nd Yeshua¦95756\nd* that I've¦95759 been¦95760 telling¦95760 you¦95761 about¦95758 is¦95752 \nd the¦95754 messiah¦95754\nd*.”
\v 4 Some¦95763 of¦95764 them¦95765 were¦95766 persuaded¦95766 and¦95767 joined¦95768 with¦95770 Paul¦95770 and¦95771 Silas¦95773, along with a¦95783 big¦95784 group of¦95777 godly Greeks¦95781 and¦95788 quite a¦95792 few¦95792 prominent women¦95786.
\p
\v 5 But¦95796 some of the¦95797 other Jews¦95799 were¦95793 envious¦95793 \add of them\add*, and¦95800 enlisted some¦95809 of¦95805 the troublemakers from the¦95805 marketplaces¦95806 to form¦95814 a¦95814 mob¦95814. They¦95815 stirred up all the¦95816 people, and¦95818 \add ≈looking¦95824 for¦95824\add* \add @Paul¦95825 and¦95825 Silas¦95825\add* so they could bring¦95827 them out¦95827, arrived at the¦95830 house¦95822 of¦95823 a man¦95808 named Jason.
\v 6 But when they realised that¦95852 \add @Paul¦95835 and¦95835 Silas¦95835\add* weren't there, they¦95836 dragged¦95836 Jason and¦95841 some¦95842 other believers¦95844 off to the¦95846 city¦95847 leaders, shouting¦95848, “Those¦95857 two men who've gone around upsetting¦95856 the¦95854 whole world¦95855 have \add now\add* come¦95861 here¦95860 as well
\v 7 and Jason has¦95863 welcomed¦95863 them \add into his house\add*. They rebel against Caesar's¦95871 decrees¦95870 and claim that \nd Yeshua¦95878\nd* is a rival king¦95873.”
\v 8 They¦95880 stirred up the¦95883 crowd¦95885 and¦95887 the¦95889 city¦95891 leaders with these¦95894 accusations,
\v 9 \add ≈so¦95895\add* the¦95897 leaders collected a heavy fine from¦95899 Jason and the others, and then released them¦95906.
\s1 Many new believers in Berea
