\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦95908\add* the¦95907 believers¦95909 immediately¦95910 sent¦95915 Paul¦95918 and¦95919 Silas¦95921 off during the night¦95914 to¦95923 go¦95933 to Berea¦95924. In¦95927 Berea they also attended at the¦95928 \add ≈Jewish¦95929 meeting¦95929 hall¦95929\add*
\v 11 and¦95935 this group were¦95936 more¦95938 upper-class than¦95938 the¦95939 congregation in¦95940 Thessalonica¦95942. They eagerly accepted¦95944 the¦95945 message¦95946 and examined¦95953 the¦95954 scriptures¦95955 every¦95951 day¦95952 to check if¦95956 what was being taught matched what was written there.
\v 12 Because it did, many¦95963 of the¦95979 people¦95985 believed¦95969 including¦95973 quite a¦95990 few¦95990 of¦95974 the¦95974 prominent¦95981 Greeks.
\v 13 But¦95992 when¦95991 the¦95994 Jews¦95998 from¦95995 Thessalonica¦95997 \add ≈found¦95993 out\add* that¦95999 \nd God's¦96011\nd* message¦96009 was¦96004 also being proclaimed¦96004 by¦96005 Paul¦96007 there¦96021 in¦96001 Berea¦96003, they¦96018 \add soon\add* turned up to agitate¦96022 and¦96023 stir the¦96025 crowds¦96026.
\v 14 \add ≈So¦96030\add* the¦96037 believers¦96038 immediately¦96029 sent¦96036 Paul¦96035 off to the¦96045 coast, but¦96050 Silas¦96054 and¦96055 Timothy¦96057 both¦96053 stayed¦96047.
\v 15 The ones guiding Paul¦96063 took¦96064 him to¦96066 Athens¦96067 before they headed back with \add &his¦96082\add* instructions¦96082 for¦96085 Silas¦96087 and¦96088 Timothy¦96090 to come¦96097 and join him¦96099 \add again\add* as soon¦96095 as possible.
\s1 People of Athens like new ideas
