\p
\v 16 While Paul¦96110 stayed in¦96101 Athens¦96104 waiting¦96105 for them¦96107, he was¦96111 upset in¦96115 his¦96114 spirit¦96113 as he observed¦96118 how idolatrous¦96119 the¦96121 people were¦96120.
\v 17 So¦96125 while he¦96123 stayed busy \add ≈having discussions¦96123\add* with¦96129 the¦96129 Jews¦96130 and¦96131 other worshippers from the¦96132 \add ≈meeting¦96128 hall¦96128\add*, he also¦96134 spent time every¦96140 day¦96141 with¦96142 anyone¦96124 who just happened¦96144 to¦96144 be¦96144 around in the¦96137 marketplace¦96138.
\v 18 Some¦96145 of¦96148 the¦96148 Epicurean and¦96150 Stoic philosophers¦96153 enjoyed discussing things with¦96156 him¦96156, but¦96157 others just mocked him, “What¦96160 does this¦96166 babbler¦96165 want¦96162 to¦96167 talk about \add now\add*?”
\p But¦96170 others¦96169 said, “Seems that he's¦96173 talking about¦96171 strange¦96171 demons¦96172,” because¦96176 he¦96183 was¦96183 preaching¦96183 the¦96177 good¦96183 message¦96183 about \nd Yeshua¦96178\nd* and¦96179 \add ≈coming back to life\add*.
\v 19 \add ≈So¦96188\add* they grabbed¦96185 him and brought¦96199 him to¦96195 the¦96196 Aries¦96197 Hill¦96198 \add where the council sat\add* and asked¦96203, “Are¦96204 we¦96204 allowed to¦96205 know¦96205 what¦96206 this¦96209 new¦96208 teaching¦96216 that¦96210 you're bringing is¦96214 about¦96192?
\v 20 It seems that you¦96221 have some¦96219 surprising¦96217 ideas for our ears¦96227, so¦96230 we¦96229 want¦96229 to¦96231 hear what¦96233 it's all¦96233 about.”
\v 21 (Everyone¦96241 in Athens¦96239 and¦96242 even visitors¦96244 often took the¦96243 opportunity¦96251 either to¦96253 explain or¦96255 to¦96257 listen¦96257 to any¦96258 new things.)
\p
\v 22 \add ≈So¦96261\add* Paul¦96263 stood¦96260 up in¦96264 the¦96265 middle¦96265 of¦96266 the gathering on the hill¦96268 and spoke, “Men¦96271 of Athens¦96272, I've¦96278 noticed how¦96275 you¦96277 all¦96277 are very religious,
\v 23 because¦96280 as I was looking around and¦96281 observing¦96283 your¦96287 objects¦96286 of¦96286 worship¦96286, I¦96288 even¦96289 discovered¦96288 an¦96290 altar¦96290 that¦96292 was¦96295 inscribed¦96295, ‘To¦96296 the unknown¦96296 \nd god¦96297\nd*.’ So¦96300 without knowing¦96301 it, you already worship this¦96303 \nd God\nd* that I'm¦96305 going to¦96307 tell you¦96307 about.
\v 24 This¦96320 \nd God¦96310\nd* who created¦96312 the¦96313 earth¦96314 and¦96315 everything in¦96318 it¦96319 is¦96325 \nd Yahweh¦96326\nd* who's over heaven¦96321 and¦96322 earth¦96323. He doesn't live¦96331 in¦96328 man-made temples¦96330
\v 25 nor¦96335 can he be¦96341 repaired by¦96336 any human¦96338 hands¦96337 and he doesn't need¦96343 to be fed. \add On the contrary\add*, he's¦96346 the one who gives¦96349 life¦96352 and¦96353 breath¦96354 and¦96356 who gives us everything that we need.
\v 26 From \add ≈one¦96362 man¦96362\add* he¦96359 made¦96359 every¦96364 nationality¦96365 that lives¦96368 across all¦96370 the earth¦96376 and designated¦96377 their boundaries¦96384 and their¦96388 futures.
\v 27 He made them so that they would try to¦96390 discover \nd God¦96393\nd*, and if¦96397 they¦96400 did search for¦96401 him¦96401 they might¦96405 find¦96405 him as he's not¦96411 far¦96412 from¦96414 any one¦96415 of¦96418 us¦96418
\v 28 because¦96423
\q1 ‘We¦96424 live¦96424 in¦96420 him¦96421 and¦96425 are¦96426 moved¦96426 by him and¦96427 exist through him.’
\m Even some¦96435 of¦96436 your own poets¦96441 wrote,
\q1 ‘We¦96448 are¦96448 all¦96439 descended¦96447 from just one.’
\m
\v 29 So¦96450 since we are¦96451 \nd God's¦96453\nd* offspring, we¦96455 shouldn't¦96454 be¦96456 putting gold¦96458 or¦96460 silver¦96462 or¦96463 stone¦96464 craftsmanship¦96466 in the¦96466 same class as the¦96471 divine¦96472.
\v 30 In fact \nd God¦96485\nd* overlooked¦96483 times¦96478 of¦96480 such ignorance¦96480 in the past, but now¦96487 he's¦96488 informing everyone and requiring them to¦96497 repent¦96497
\v 31 because he's¦96500 set¦96500 a¦96502 date¦96502 for when he's¦96505 going¦96505 to¦96506 be¦96506 fairly judging¦96506 the¦96508 world¦96509. He's already appointed the judge who¦96515 everyone¦96520 can have faith¦96517 in¦96510 because he¦96516 \add ≈brought¦96518 him¦96522 back to life\add* from¦96523 the¦96524 dead¦96524.
\p
\v 32 When¦96526 they heard¦96525 about¦96525 a¦96527 dead¦96528 \add >person\add* \add ≈coming back to life\add*, some started mocking¦96531 but others¦96533 said¦96534, “We'd¦96535 like to hear¦96535 more about¦96538 this¦96539 from¦96536 you¦96536 another time.”
\v 33 So¦96543 Paul¦96545 left¦96546 at that stage
\v 34 but¦96551 some¦96550 people¦96552 joined¦96553 with him¦96555 and believed¦96556, including Dionysius¦96560 who was a council member, a¦96566 woman¦96566 named¦96567 Damaris¦96568, and¦96569 others¦96570 as well.
\c 18
