\v 14 But¦96926 as Paul¦96928 opened¦96929 his¦96930 mouth¦96931 to speak, Gallio¦96934 said¦96932 to¦96935 the¦96936 Jews¦96937, “I would have accepted this charge if¦96938 it¦96942 was¦96942 a¦96945 serious wrong¦96944 or¦96946 evil¦96948 crime¦96947 and would have listened to¦96952 you¦96956 Jews.
\v 15 However, since it's¦96963 a \add #question¦96961\add* about¦96964 a¦96965 message¦96965 and¦96966 names¦96967 and¦96968 your own law¦96969, you all can see¦96973 to¦96973 it¦96973 yourselves¦96974 because I¦96977 don't¦96979 want¦96981 to¦96982 get involved in judging¦96975 things like that¦96970.”
\v 16 \add ≈So¦96983\add* he¦96985 sent them¦96986 away¦96985 from¦96987 the¦96988 tribunal¦96989,
\v 17 but¦96992 they grabbed¦96991 Sosthenes¦96997, the¦96998 leader¦96999 from the \add ≈meeting¦96999 hall¦96999\add*, and beat him up right there \add ≈in¦97001 front¦97001 of¦97001\add* the¦97002 tribunal¦97003. But¦97004 Gallio¦97009 took¦96991 action to stop them.
